A1. This causes many a downfall. ~ BANANA
A6. A scout for Sing Sing's baseball team. ~ SLEUTH
A11. This is hard and unrefined. ~ ORE
A12. A dumb-belle (so thinks little brother). ~ SIS
A14. Poison to many. ~ IVY
A15. Part of the verb "to be." ~ IS
A17. The kind of people who become after-dinner speakers. ~ TALKATIVE
A20. This never means to be off. ~ ON
A21. An ornament-holder for women. ~ EAR
A23. A gold-headed parrakeet of Brazil. ~ TUI
A24. This means gold to some. ~ ORE
A25. You do this when you put two and two together. ~ ADD
A26. What did Cupid do when Psyche lit the light? ~ FLEW
A28. At what place did Hamlet last see Yorick? ~ GRAVE
A30. This goes around in movie palaces. ~ REEL
A31. You're lucky if you can keep your stock in this condition. ~ PAR
A33. This is always on foot. ~ TOE
A34. This is good as far as it goes. ~ CAR
A35. This would awaken anyone's curiosity. ~ CURIO
A37. You'll find this at the end of the journey-that is if you don't drive. ~ DEPOT
A39. Any kid would like to make a hit with this. ~ BAT
A40. How did the ploughman get home in Gray's Elegy? ~ PLODDED
A41. An American poet who lived in the first part of the 19th century. ~ POE
A42. What did Paul Revere do on his midnight ride? ~ WAKED
A44. What adjective means "powdery"—like meal? ~ MEALY
A47. The first name of a famous charioteer. ~ BEN
A48. Seen in any American landscape (Plural) ~ ADS
A50. A good place to get a drink. ~ SPA
A52. Depend. ~ RELY
A54. A great dramatist. ~ IBSEN
A56. What is hard on the back—tackle this one? (plural.) ~ ENDS
A58. This is often picked on by the younger generation. ~ UKE
A59. A period. ~ ERA
A60. Good for a hold-up. ~ DAM
A62. If you fill this in properly it will be pronounced the same as "ease." ~ EEE
A63. Objective pronoun. ~ ME
A64. What many a man does when his mother-in-law arrives. ~ EVACUATES
A67. French conjunction. ~ ET
A68. Part of the verb "to be." ~ ARE
A69. Close relations. ~ KIN
A70. At least one is found on any family tree. ~ NUT
A72. What reformers work for ~ SALARY
A73. What Lindy refuses to take for any girl. ~ TUMBLE

D1. These have very few words. ~ BRIEFS
D2. A feminine reply that usually means the exact opposite. ~ NO
D3. Something hard to find in artist's studios. ~ ART
D4. What the well-dressed girl is. ~ NEAT
D5. By way of ~ VIA
D7. What you do if you're not a dead one. ~ LIVE
